<title>USA: Supertyphoon threatens southern Japan - WSC.</title>
<headline>Supertyphoon threatens southern Japan - WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Supertyphoon Rosie, in the Pacific Ocean south of Japan, is expected to pass east of Okinawa but threatens southern Japan, independent forecaster Weather Services Corp said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The storm, with 160 mph winds, is expected to turn to the north and landfall should occur in 60-72 hours in Kyushu.</p>
<p>Top winds at the time of landfall are expected to be near 125 mph.</p>
<p>Rosie has the potential to bring significant damage to southern Japan, WSC said.</p>
